00:00:49.943 --> 00:00:50.776
I thought that was so cool.

00:00:50.776 --> 00:00:52.680
- I did!
when I did nine to five.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.420
Back 40 what?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.130
Two years ago or so.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.369
I just watched it on
the set and I played my.

00:00:58.369 --> 00:00:59.602
(nails clicking)

00:00:59.602 --> 00:01:00.435
My nails.

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:02.076
(audience cheers)

00:01:02.076 --> 00:01:03.390
- I can't, look, these
are single mama nails.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.223
- I know.

00:01:04.223 --> 00:01:05.056
Well, these are acrylics.

00:01:05.056 --> 00:01:05.889
- These are gross.

00:01:05.889 --> 00:01:07.139
- You gotta have falsies.

00:01:07.139 --> 00:01:08.610
(laughing)

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.350
Anyway, I was playing my acrylic nails

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.140
and I watched all the
things going on on the set

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.360
and so I just watched all the girls

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.730
doing whatever they did and
it was about working women.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.140
- Yeah.
- So when I wrote the song,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.130
got ready to record it.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.786
I thought how cool would it
be to invite all the women?

00:01:22.786 --> 00:01:24.780
- Yeah.
- That worked in the offices

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.610
and all the people on the
set and all the girls.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:27.870
- You keep it real.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.310
- Yeah.
So they all sang on it

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:30.611
and they got credit.

00:01:30.611 --> 00:01:31.444
- I love that.
- I got credit

00:01:31.444 --> 00:01:33.617
for playing nails.
(laughing)

00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:34.450
I did.
- I love that.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:35.403
I love it.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.953
All right so.
Oh, thank you so much Justin.

00:01:38.953 --> 00:01:41.239
Give it up for Justin.
(Claps)

00:01:41.239 --> 00:01:42.090
(audience cheering)

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.860
Dolly is so special to me, y'all.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.630
And she's special to the entire show.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.610
And I apologize that you're
standing here for this

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.660
'cause it's probably awkward for you.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.100
But I'm gonna embarrass
you just for a minute

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.660
or just float your boat.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.950
So this isn't the first time

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.960
that I've sung nine to five on this stage.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.750
In fact, that song was
my very first Kelly Yoki

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.889
on this show, for this whole show.

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:00.722
- Oh, I didn't know that!

00:02:00.722 --> 00:02:01.555
- Yeah.
Season one.

00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:02.388
It was our very first one.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.221
- Well, I'm honored.
- Yeah.

00:02:03.221 --> 00:02:04.980
And like you, you said you had real,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.150
like workers in the video.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.040
So did we.
We had real police women.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.071
We had real fire women.

00:02:09.071 --> 00:02:10.451
- Oh yeah, I see them there.

00:02:10.451 --> 00:02:12.180
Oh, look at that.
- It was really cool.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.020
And, and I'm so excited though
to just sing that with you

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.070
and also just to have you here.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:17.903
We're super honored.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.220
- Well, I have always said we
would do a great show together

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:22.160
and I think we're going to.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.850
'Cause I just relate to you so much.

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.860
I just think you're so real and so fun.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.292
And everybody just loves you.

00:02:27.292 --> 00:02:28.380
- That's what I think about you!

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.305
- Well, then that's why
we're gonna have on the show.

00:02:30.305 --> 00:02:31.926
(laughs)
(audience cheering)

00:02:31.926 --> 00:02:33.300
- Well, we're blessed to have Dolly

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.010
for the whole hour, everybody.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.177
She is a legend.
(audience cheering)

00:02:36.177 --> 00:02:37.356
In music, in fashion.

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:39.480
She's got two musical collections out now.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.313
One is called

00:02:40.313 --> 00:02:42.600
the "Holly Dolly Christmas
Ultimate Deluxe Edition".

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.927
My God, you smell so good.

00:02:43.927 --> 00:02:46.470
The other, I'm just taking it in.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.303
The other is

00:02:47.303 --> 00:02:49.860
"Diamonds and Rhinestones,
The Greatest Hits Collection"

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.630
Both are available wherever
you get your music,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.920
you'll gotta get them.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.870
But Dolly is a worldwide
inspiration for her work

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.980
as a humanitarian as well.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.030
That's why she's even cooler.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.440
She just didn't stop there with music.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.970
Nope.
That's why

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.410
we're introducing a new theme,

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.610
that's brand new for our show.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.920
And it celebrates the
people behind the art

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:05.910
that they create.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.923
So it starts with Dolly and
it's called "More Than Music".

00:03:08.923 --> 00:03:10.342
(gentle music)

00:03:10.342 --> 00:03:14.497
♪ More than music. ♪

00:03:14.497 --> 00:03:15.690
- Okay.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.130
Oh and I got my own cup.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.390
- You have your own cup.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.223
- I just love this.

00:03:19.223 --> 00:03:20.056
- I know.

00:03:20.056 --> 00:03:20.889
Ooh, and I have this

00:03:20.889 --> 00:03:22.110
and I've got so many things
over here I'm gonna talk about.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.300
Well wait, I have to say congrats.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.304
You were just inducted into
the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.

00:03:26.304 --> 00:03:27.137
- I know!

00:03:27.137 --> 00:03:29.383
(Kelly claps)
(audience cheering)

00:03:29.383 --> 00:03:30.216
- I wanna see, can I see it?

00:03:30.216 --> 00:03:32.657
- I know.
I brought this for the show.

00:03:32.657 --> 00:03:35.730
This is my rock and roll
and I just wanna share this

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.783
with you until you get
your own and you will.

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.201
- Oh, I will not but I love you.

00:03:39.201 --> 00:03:40.034
(laughs)

00:03:40.034 --> 00:03:41.220
- Yes, you will.
You will!

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.080
- You are so.
I think you have to.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.520
Well, it's funny, I was literally talking

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.310
to my producer this
morning and I was like,

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.350
we throw around the word icon a lot.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.210
Like I feel like everybody's an icon now.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.800
Like, you know, everybody's
like, oh she's an icon.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.000
I'm like, no, you have to earn that

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.920
and you actually earned that.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.120
And it's like you, that's
why I loved your response.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.550
I loved your response 'cause
you were like, well, wait what?

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.080
Rock and roll?
Like I'm country music.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.190
But you are rock and roll.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.750
The fact that you're a pioneer for women,

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.250
you've opened the doors for so many of us

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.410
to be able to be
vulnerable as songwriters.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.430
But I don't know, does it make,

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.320
does it weird you out
to be labeled an icon?

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.153
Does it?

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.410
- Well, I always think of myself more

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:18.240
as an eyesore than an icon.
(laughs)

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.073
- Well, I wish you.

00:04:19.073 --> 00:04:20.737
- But actually, but you know,

00:04:20.737 --> 00:04:23.280
I used to think when I was young

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.410
if I made it like I'd hoped I would.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.790
- Yeah.
- How people would remember me

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.660
when I was older.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.010
Now I'm older

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:32.520
and it's really nice to look
back and think that, you know

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.770
I might have done something
that's helped inspire.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:35.603
- Oh my God.
So many thing.

00:04:35.603 --> 00:04:36.630
- Some, you know, some other people.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.690
And when I got into the
Rock and Roll Hall of Fame

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.400
when they talked about that,

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.520
I didn't realize that it was
more than just that to me.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.710
I always thought about the
Rock and Roll Hall of Fame

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:49.410
being for people to spend
their life in rock music.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:50.670
- Yeah.
- Like country music

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.990
and you don't see Led Zeppelin

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.430
in the country Music Hall of Fame.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.720
- Yeah.
- You know, so I,

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.430
when they first said that, I thought,

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.770
well, you know, I don't
know that I belong there

00:04:58.770 --> 00:04:59.880
and I didn't wanna take votes

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.560
from other people that
had spent their life.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.240
And that's kinda how I felt.
- Which is so dolly.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.830
- But I.
- Who says that!

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.900
- But still, I honestly thought that.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.655
But then later I saw that it
was for people also that have,

00:05:09.655 --> 00:05:11.340
you know, influenced other people.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:14.340
And I did say I would accept
it gracefully and humbly

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.652
and I did and I was very honored.

00:05:16.652 --> 00:05:18.930
- But you did something even cooler.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.217
You actually wrote like
a rock and roll song.

00:05:20.217 --> 00:05:22.740
- I did.
I wrote a song for the show

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.360
about my whole experience about that.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.602
It's called, I've been,
it's called "Rockin' It"

00:05:26.602 --> 00:05:27.435
'Cause I've been rocking it.

00:05:27.435 --> 00:05:28.759
I grew up loving Elvis

00:05:28.759 --> 00:05:31.636
and while Man Jerry Lee,
Chuck Barry, little Richard

00:05:31.636 --> 00:05:34.650
they had a cast of spell on me

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.320
and Carl Perkins in them Blue Swag shoes

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.970
had no place on the farm.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:39.803
But there's better

00:05:39.803 --> 00:05:42.492
than them Brogans I was
wearing around the barn.

00:05:42.492 --> 00:05:44.809
♪ So I've been rocking, rocking, rocking ♪

00:05:44.809 --> 00:05:46.652
♪ since the day I was born. ♪

00:05:46.652 --> 00:05:50.251
♪ I'll be rocking till the day I'm gone. ♪

00:05:50.251 --> 00:05:53.852
♪ 'Cause I got rocking roll
down in my country soul. ♪

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:56.460
♪ And I'll be rocking it
till the cows come home. ♪

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.055
- I love that!

00:05:58.055 --> 00:06:00.037
(laughs)
(audience cheering)

00:06:00.037 --> 00:06:00.870
That's so perfect.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:01.703
- So yeah.

00:06:01.703 --> 00:06:04.230
I'll go ahead and I'll
talk about the whole thing.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.880
How, you know, how they, you know,

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.290
they put me in the Hall of Fame.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.390
So guess, it ain't no
shame, is there, you know.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.850
But since I heard the big news,
I ain't never been the same.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.620
Cause they done gone and put me

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:16.470
in the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:17.880
It's a dangerous thing.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.560
But I was honored and I'm proud.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.550
- I love that.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.012
And it's so cool though how you do,

00:06:22.012 --> 00:06:24.300
you're so respectful of other artists

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.133
and all their hard work.

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:26.340
But at the same time you're like

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.540
'cause you're doing an album now.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.373
Like a rock album.

00:06:28.373 --> 00:06:31.903
- I'm doing a rock album now.
I'm calling in Rock Star.

00:06:31.903 --> 00:06:33.569
Rock Star.
- I love it.

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:35.360
- Just for fun.
But I'm actually,

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.170
I'm doing a classic songs

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.660
and I'm using a lot of
the classic artists too

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.730
to sing on some of the songs with me so.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:42.563
- Wow.

00:06:42.563 --> 00:06:43.770
- So I'm looking forward to that.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.676
So this gonna come out next year.

00:06:45.676 --> 00:06:47.244
♪ Go, tell it, tell it. ♪

00:06:47.244 --> 00:06:48.975
♪ Go, tell it, tell it. ♪

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.763
♪ Go, tell it, tell it. ♪

00:06:50.763 --> 00:06:52.672
♪ Go, tell it, tell it. ♪

